            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Origanum onites, the Cretan oregano,{{citation needed|date=May 2016}} Greek oregano, pot marjoram or Ellinikí rίgani in Greek (Ελληνική ρίγανη), is a plant species in the genus Origanum found in Sicily, Greece and Turkey. It has similar flavors as common oregano. It has antimicrobial activities."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Chemistry\nThe plant contains the chemical compounds thymol, carvacrol and cedrol.{{citation needed|date=September 2016}}"
          }
        ]
      }
